{"id": "EUVD-2026-99254", "enisaUuid": "e2af95cf-f59c-3359-b967-5e9e8c16bc4c", "description": "Stonewuu ai-fusion-video through 1.2.0 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability that allows authenticated users to read other users' generation results by supplying arbitrary task ids. Attackers can enumerate auto-increment task ids on the image and video /items endpoints to obtain other users' generated images, videos, and output metadata.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T15:57:54", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/ai-fusion-video-broken-access-control-and-upload-path-traversal", "https://github.com/Stonewuu/ai-fusion-video/blob/v1.2.0/ai-fusion-video/src/main/java/com/stonewu/fusion/controller/generation/ImageGenerationController.java#L50-L54", "https://github.com/Stonewuu/ai-fusion-video/blob/v1.2.0/ai-fusion-video/src/main/java/com/stonewu/fusion/controller/generation/VideoGenerationController.java#L49-L53", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ai-fusion-video-through-1.2.0-insecure-direct-object-reference-in-generation-task-item-endpoints"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2w44-g53g-ccjh", "CVE-2026-110213"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "59791f26-e448-33f9-8d74-656fb74611d8", "product": {"name": "ai-fusion-video", "vendor": {"name": "Stonewuu"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "884a8123-b42f-37aa-a27d-0485303f06a6", "vendor": {"name": "Stonewuu"}}], "isExploited": false}